// `s.localeCompare(t)` on every character of its table (std/lang/string/collate_table.velt) but
// the four that stand for three or more collation elements (`¼`, `½`, `¾`, `ϗ`), listed in
// Node's order (`Intl.Collator("und")`, ICU 77.1). For each neighbouring pair x, y it prints three
// signs: x vs y; x + "b" vs y + "a", which is ">" only when x and y have the same base letters
// (primary weights); and x + "á" vs y + "a", ">" only when their accents (secondary weights) are
// equal too. So a wrong rank at any level in the table changes a sign. The expected output is
// Node's where Node and the Rust that velt_rt had agree, which is on all 4113 comparisons
// but 12: the suffixed pairs of `‥` and `…` and of the primes `′` `″` `‴` `⁗` and `‵` `‶`
// `‷`, which ICU reads as two or more of one element. There it is the old Rust's, which the
// port follows.

